meta {
  name: Verify Webhook Signature
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/__webhook_receiver_docs_only__
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
  X-Externa-Event-Id: evt_01example
  X-Externa-Timestamp: 1721822400
  X-Externa-Signature: sha256=REPLACE_WITH_HMAC
}

body:json {
  {
    "id": "evt_01example",
    "type": "item.updated",
    "created_at": "2026-07-24T12:00:00Z",
    "data": {
      "collection_id": 1,
      "collection_slug": "posts",
      "item_id": 42
    }
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

tests {
  test("placeholder URL is not an Externa route (404)", function () {
    // Docs-only helper: default path does not exist on externa-core.
    // After you point the URL at your receiver, loosen/remove this assertion.
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(404);
  });
}

docs {
  # Verify webhook signature
  
  Externa **outbound** webhooks are Externa → **your** URL. There is no Externa route to call for receiving them.
  
  This request is a **docs helper**: sample envelope + signing notes. It is **not** a Public API endpoint.
  
  ## Placeholder URL (intentional)
  
  Default URL: `{{base_url}}/__webhook_receiver_docs_only__`
  
  That path does **not** exist on externa-core. Sending as-is returns **404**. Replace the URL with:
  
  - your local receiver, or
  - a temporary https://webhook.site URL
  
  then POST this sample to practice verifying `X-Externa-Signature`.
  
  Full docs: [Outbound webhooks](https://github.com/qiick-io/externa-docs/blob/main/src/app/docs/webhooks/page.md) (`/docs/webhooks`)
  
  ## Headers Externa sends
  
  | Header | Meaning |
  |--------|---------|
  | `X-Externa-Signature` | `sha256=` + HMAC-SHA256(raw body, project webhook secret) |
  | `X-Externa-Event-Id` | Event id (`evt_...`) |
  | `X-Externa-Timestamp` | Unix seconds at delivery time |
  | `User-Agent` | `Externa-Webhooks/1.0` |
  
  ## Sign / verify (Node)
  
  Sign the **exact raw request body bytes** (not a re-serialized JSON object):
  
      const crypto = require('crypto')
      const expected = 'sha256=' + crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(rawBody).digest('hex')
      crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(expected), Buffer.from(header))
  
  1. Set `webhook_secret` (collection `.env` → `EXTERNA_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) to the Project settings secret  
  2. Compute `expected` over this request’s raw JSON body  
  3. Paste it into `X-Externa-Signature` above  
  4. Change the URL to your receiver and Send  
  
  ## Env vars
  
  | Variable | Purpose |
  |----------|---------|
  | `webhook_secret` | Same secret as Settings → Project → webhook secret |
  
  ## Real delivery from Externa (preferred smoke test)
  
  1. Settings → Project → Webhook URL + Generate secret → Save  
  2. Run a queue worker  
  3. **Send test event** (`ping`) or create/update an item  
  4. Inspect the POST on webhook.site / your receiver  
  
  Events: `item.*`, `file.*`, `collection.*`, `ping` — see externa-docs `/docs/webhooks`.
}
